HOLD-MARKER REGEX -- CONTROLS, and the corrections that produced this version

*** THE FIRST TWO VERSIONS OF THIS FILE BOTH CARRIED A FALSE WARRANT, AND BOTH WERE CAUGHT
BY SEATS RATHER THAN BY ME. ***

v1  three controls, one of them VACUOUS: the `ledgerstatelies` quotation lives in a
    row-level `state_note`, and held_rows() walks only entries[].note -- so it was never
    fed to the regex and could not fail.  Found by grok mid-answer; deepseek and minimax
    reached the same conclusion from the packet alone.
v2  class `[a-z0-9_,\s]+?`.  MEASURED to span newlines.  Its comment claimed the quotation
    was a 'built-in negative control' -- opus5 measured that swapping in the permissive
    `([^]]+?)`, or `(.+?)` with DOTALL, passes every control and renders sgirekills
    BYTE-IDENTICALLY.  The comment asserted a proof that does not exist.
    It also claimed 'every defang note quotes the literal it refutes'.  Counted in
    entries[].note: 9 live literals, ALL REAL MARKERS, 0 quotations, vs 31 defanged
    spellings.  The convention REWRITES; it does not quote.
v3  strict id-list `([a-z0-9_]+(?:[ 	]*,[ 	]*[a-z0-9_]+)*)`, adopted from opus5.

CONTROLS, injected into an ENTRY note where held_rows() actually looks:

  POSITIVE  one-seat marker                    MATCHED  [assess:opus5]
  POSITIVE  two-seat marker                    MATCHED  [assess:codex,opus5]
  POSITIVE  seven-seat marker                  MATCHED  [all seven]
  POSITIVE  comma WITHOUT space (opus5,codex)   MATCHED  [assess:codex,opus5]
            <- added after the fable5 seat found the smallest SURVIVING break against the
               rebuilt controls: `split(",")` -> `split(", ")`.  Measured: under that mutant
               a no-space marker collapses to ONE seat (`opus5,codex`) while the with-space
               control still renders correctly -- so the with-space row alone cannot kill it.
               The token grammar makes the separator explicit; this row proves the split
               agrees with it.
  NEGATIVE  newline-spanning                   no match
  NEGATIVE  defanged form                      no match
  NEGATIVE  punctuation inside                 no match
  NEGATIVE  hyphenated id (kimi-k3)            no match   <- see LIMIT 2

DOCUMENTED RESIDUAL, not a failure:
  a note QUOTING a real, well-formed marker MATCHES.  Any regex that recognises real
  markers recognises quotations of them; the remedy is DEFANGING the quotation, which is
  what the carrier already prescribes.  Recorded so a future reader does not read it as
  an escape.

*** ONE OF opus5's CLAIMS DID NOT REPRODUCE, AND IT IS RECORDED BECAUSE A SEAT'S FINDING
GETS CHECKED TOO. ***  It reported that `ledgerstatelies`' own sentence would manufacture a
hold naming seats `and, not, a, panel` if moved into an entry note.  Tested against the REAL
prose rather than a constructed one: it reads

      ... is a **`[HELD AWAITING SEAT:` MARKER** -- a record that the seat is OUTSTANDING ...

A BACKTICK follows the colon, so NEITHER the loose class NOR the strict one matches it, in
any field.  My own first attempt to reproduce it was worse: I invented a 'phantom' that was
a syntactically PERFECT marker, so it matched and proved nothing.  The general point stands
-- a loose class can match prose -- but this instance is not an example of it.

LIMITS, stated rather than discovered later:
  1. A real marker WRAPPED ACROSS LINES is invisible.  Deliberate: admitting newlines
     re-opens the phantom surface.  Markers are generated on one line.
  2. A hyphenated transport name (`kimi-k3`) would be invisible.  No ledger seat id needs
     one today -- CHECKED, not assumed -- but a future substitute transport would.

*** THE REAL DETECTOR IS `--check`, NOT THESE CONTROLS.  Measured by opus5. ***
Of nine mutants it built, only reverting the comma is killed by the controls; the 4-character
`.split(",")[:1]` passes all of them while collapsing a seven-seat hold to one seat -- the
very defect this change repairs, re-opened with the guard intact.  Section I2
(`gen_codex_wall.py --check` against the committed `fable_queue.md`) kills that one and two
more.  On HEAD it reports: CODEX_WALL_OK  8 held stages, section matches the ledger.

TWO EQUIVALENT MUTANTS (results, not noise, per the mutant-that-will-not-die rule):
  * dropping the non-greedy `?` -- `]` is not in the class, so greedy and lazy stop at the
    same place;
  * inverting `if seat and s != seat` -- every call site passes seat=None (block() and
    main(); nothing else imports held_rows), so that line is DEAD at every call site.

HOLDMARKER_CONTROLS_DONE  CONTROLS PASS; RESIDUAL AND TWO LIMITS DOCUMENTED ABOVE
